From f92d2932cd69c2515cb4ac829b9cba3b9b5ec127 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: C0fuge <189659128+C0fuge@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:20:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Remember failed DataNodes process-wide with an expiry
 (input.deadnode.ttl)

InputStreamImpl forgets a failed DataNode at every block (seekToBlock clears
failedNodes) and in every new stream. While a DataNode is silently lost (and
the namenode still lists it, ~10.5 min), every block / seek / file whose
replica order starts with it pays the connect or read timeout again. Readers
that seek a lot (DuckDB parquet) then take 24-121 s for a scan instead of
1-4 s.

New: DeadNodes, a process-wide list keyed by DataNode UUID@ip:xferPort.
A node whose remote block reader fails (setup timeout / IO error, or a read
error mid-block) is remembered for input.deadnode.ttl ms (default 60000,
0 = off = old behaviour). choseBestNode prefers replicas that are neither
failed for the block nor on the list; a listed node is still tried when it
is the only replica left. A successful block reader setup on a node removes
it at once. EC (striped) reads are unchanged.
